# Normalize all text files to LF in the repo
* text=auto eol=lf

# eva#266: `agent/memory/evolution/lessons.md` deliberately declares NO merge
# driver. `merge=union` was proposed (and tried) to auto-resolve the common
# case — two independent writers appending near the file's end — but it removes
# the `mergeStateStatus: DIRTY` signal, and DIRTY is the ONLY trigger for
# eva-conflict-scan.yml's `try_renumber_and_rebuild` self-heal, which exists
# precisely because a textual resolve can leave a duplicate `## L-YYYY-MM-DD-NN`
# ID behind. Union-merging that case yields a clean merge carrying a colliding
# ID: the Lint & Test duplicate-ID gate turns red, and nothing heals it
# (eva-review-pr only fires on `workflow_run.conclusion == 'success'`,
# eva-fix-pr needs a review, eva-ci-failure skips non-`main` branches). Leaving
# the file conflict-prone keeps the recoverable path; the CI gate in tests.yml
# covers the semantic collision a git-level resolve can't see.
